# The browser probes each write a page next to index.html and delete it after -
# _pypage.html, _ligweb.html and so on. One survived a crash and was committed
# (_panelpic2.html, 1,022 lines of nothing).
_*.html

# ...and the same lesson three times more. A probe run by hand writes its dumps
# into whatever directory it was started from, and `git add -A` sweeps them into
# the branch: resize-fast.png and resize-full.png went in that way, and
# notes.txt was a one-line scratchpad nobody meant to keep. Write dumps
# somewhere outside the tree; if one lands here anyway, it does not become a
# commit.
#
# 🔴 AND THE LEADING SLASH IS WHY IT HAPPENED AGAIN. `/*.png` is anchored to
# the repository ROOT, so a dump written one directory down is not covered at
# all - scratch/fast.png and scratch/reb.png, 656 KB of before-and-after
# screenshots, were committed in 82058f5 past a rule written for exactly them.
# Unanchored, so it holds wherever the probe was started from; the fixtures
# this repo does keep are .cif and .pdb, and there is no .png it wants.
*.png
/notes.txt
